# module-07.http: write requests W01-W16 (VS Code "REST Client" extension).
# Use @example.com addresses only. Messages are personal data, even in a lab.
# NOTE: reconstructed by the playground author from the course's write-test list; yours wins if it differs.
@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000
# From Module 8 the owner requests also need:  X-API-Key: {{key}}
@key = your-owner-key-from-.env

### W01 A valid message -> 201, Location header, {id, sent_at}
POST {{base}}/api/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ravi Kumar", "email": "ravi@example.com", "message": "Hello from the lab" }

### W02 No email key -> 422
POST {{base}}/api/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ravi Kumar", "message": "Hello" }

### W03 "ravi-at-example" -> 422
POST {{base}}/api/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ravi Kumar", "email": "ravi-at-example", "message": "Hello" }

### W04 message of three spaces -> 422 (str_strip_whitespace turns it into "")
POST {{base}}/api/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ravi Kumar", "email": "ravi@example.com", "message": "   " }

### W05 Read messages (newest first, is_read is false not 0)
GET {{base}}/api/messages
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### W06 Mark message 1 read (send it twice: 200 both times)
PATCH {{base}}/api/messages/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{ "is_read": true }

### W07 Mark a message that is not there -> 404
PATCH {{base}}/api/messages/99999
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{ "is_read": true }

### W08 Delete message 1 -> 204, no body
DELETE {{base}}/api/messages/1
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### W09 Delete it again -> 404
DELETE {{base}}/api/messages/1
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### W10 Change only a description -> 200 (restore it afterwards)
PATCH {{base}}/api/projects/14
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{ "description": "Rolled out to the whole company." }

### W11 Give project 1 project 2's name -> 409
PATCH {{base}}/api/projects/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{ "project_name": "Branch Banking Portal" }

### W12a An empty PATCH -> 422
PATCH {{base}}/api/projects/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{}

### W12b A field that does not exist -> 422 (extra="forbid")
PATCH {{base}}/api/projects/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{ "budget": 5 }

### W13 Appointment, end BEFORE start -> 422 and NOTHING is left behind
POST {{base}}/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{
  "company_name": "Kestrel Ridge Analytics",
  "role_title": "Non-Executive Director",
  "start_date": "2026-06-01",
  "end_date": "2026-05-31",
  "project_name": "Acquisition technology due diligence",
  "skill_ids": [17],
  "headline": "Former Chief Technology Officer | Non-Executive Director, Kestrel Ridge Analytics"
}

### W14 The board appointment -> 201 with FOUR ids; then GET /api/summary -> 8 / 18 / 17 / 17 / 19 / 43.0
POST {{base}}/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{
  "company_name": "Kestrel Ridge Analytics",
  "role_title": "Non-Executive Director",
  "start_date": "2026-06-01",
  "end_date": "2029-05-31",
  "project_name": "Acquisition technology due diligence",
  "skill_ids": [17],
  "headline": "Former Chief Technology Officer | Non-Executive Director, Kestrel Ridge Analytics"
}

### W15 Send W14 again -> 409, summary unchanged
POST {{base}}/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{
  "company_name": "Kestrel Ridge Analytics",
  "role_title": "Non-Executive Director",
  "start_date": "2026-06-01",
  "end_date": "2029-05-31",
  "project_name": "Acquisition technology due diligence",
  "skill_ids": [17],
  "headline": "Former Chief Technology Officer | Non-Executive Director, Kestrel Ridge Analytics"
}

### W16 (stretch) A skill that does not exist -> predict 1452 -> 422, nothing left behind
POST {{base}}/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{
  "company_name": "Zed Labs",
  "role_title": "Advisor",
  "start_date": "2026-06-01",
  "end_date": "2027-05-31",
  "project_name": "Zed advisory",
  "skill_ids": [99]
}

### Extra: PUT is not in our spec -> 405 with an Allow header
PUT {{base}}/api/messages/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{key}}

{ "is_read": true }
